.TH SLEEP 3
.SH NAME
sleep \- suspend execution for an interval
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
unsigned
sleep(seconds)
unsigned seconds;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sleep
suspends the program for
.I seconds
seconds, or until a signal that it catches arrives. It sets the alarm
clock with
.BR alarm (2)
and waits for its signal with
.BR pause (2).
.SH "RETURN VALUES"
0.
.SH SEE ALSO
alarm(2), pause(2), signal(2)
.SH HISTORY
A
.B sleep
system call first appeared in Version 2 AT&T UNIX. In Version 7 it was
replaced by this function of the C library, built on alarm and pause.
.SH BUGS
sleep uses the alarm clock: an alarm the program had set is lost, and
its handler for SIGALRM is put back when sleep returns.
.PP
The time is counted in whole seconds by the system clock, and may be up
to a second shorter than asked for.
